      'formula.tl': `<h3>TARGET LOAD (recommended pieces to load)</h3><p>For the first hour, set target WIP to HOURLY TARGET × 1.25, then subtract opening WIP. If opening WIP already meets or exceeds this level, TARGET LOAD is 0 because a nonnegative load cannot reduce WIP.</p><p>Later hours use the shortfall from HOURLY TARGET plus a 25% buffer: round(max(0, HOURLY TARGET − previous BALANCE) × 1.25).</p><p><b>Example:</b> With a target of 85 and opening WIP of 60, round(106.25 − 60) = 46 pieces; with opening WIP 0, round(106.25) = 106 pieces.</p>`,
      'formula.load': `<h3>ACTUAL LOAD (pieces loaded)</h3><p>Pieces loaded into the sewing line during the period. The backend calculates this value; the page displays it.</p><p><b>Color shows whether loading is on target</b>, compared with TARGET LOAD.</p><ul><li><span class="hi"><b>Orange</b></span> = more than 1.25 times TARGET LOAD</li><li><span class="lo"><b>Blue</b></span> = below TARGET LOAD</li><li>White = within the acceptable range</li></ul><p><b>Example:</b> If WIP is high, TARGET LOAD is 0. Any additional load is shown in orange.</p>`,
